 thresh        EVOLVED                      SEED
           preds   corr    prec        preds   corr    prec
   0.00   116083   4144  0.0357         5112   1127  0.2205
   0.05    24120   2633  0.1092         5112   1127  0.2205
   0.10     5745   1199  0.2087         5112   1127  0.2205
   0.15     3693    893  0.2418         5112   1127  0.2205
   0.20     3625    875  0.2414         4069    967  0.2377

CURVES CROSS. Neither dominates.

The reading that matters: THE SEED HAS NO DIAL. Its curve is FLAT at
0.2205 from t=0.00 through 0.15, because its rules are the top-60
enumerated BY dev confidence -- they all clear every filter until the
threshold reaches them. 7 distinct operating points for evolved, 3 for
the seed and effectively 1.

At its own point the seed is slightly better than anything evolution
offers nearby. EVERYWHERE ELSE ON THE FRONTIER ONLY EVOLUTION HAS POINTS
AT ALL. The whole high-coverage region exists only because of evolution.

So evolution's contribution is RANGE, not a better curve. Weaker than
what I claimed in G24 and more useful: want ~1100 correct at ~22%, don't
evolve, enumerate. Want 2600 or 4100, enumeration has no setting that
reaches them.

